# Names check-doc-tokens.sh accepts although no Marble CSS defines them.
# One name per line; the rest of the line says why. Remove an entry once no doc needs it.

# IceBlue variable names, cited when comparing the two themes (iceblue-parity.md, component-design-notes.md)
--zk-base-border-color
--zk-base-border-radius
--zk-base-font-size
--zk-base-popup-z-index
--zk-base-title-font-family
--zk-border-radius-large
--zk-border-radius-small
--zk-color-primary-dark
--zk-messagebox-icon-size
--zk-tabbox-icon-size

# Placeholders and examples that name no real token
--zk-color-x            placeholder (css-audit.md)
--zk-spacing-N          placeholder for a spacing step
--zk-token              placeholder (tokens.md)
--zk-font-weight-medium a token an agent once invented; tokens.md cites it as the warning
--zk-window-title-size  illustrative slot (component-theme-variables.md)
--zk-grid-header-fill   a token proposed for a future variant (DESIGN.md)
--zk-grid-fg            named in _component-theme.css to say it does not exist
--zk-button             shorthand for the --zk-button-* family in a comment
--zk-codeeditor-active-line  a ZK-documented hook Marble deliberately leaves undeclared (codeeditor.md)

# Not a token
--zk-source             a command-line flag of audit-css.sh
